ANSWERS=['(a) −1/4; (b) 9/4; (c) 1/2; (d) −1; (e) 1; (f) 1; (g) 0; (h) 0.','(a) −∞, no finite limit; (b) −1/9; (c) 1/(2√5).','(a) 5; (b) −7; (c) 0.','(a) 38600/7 ≈ Rs 5514.29; (b) 38600/7 ≈ Rs 5514.29; (c) Rs 5200.','(a) −1/4; (b) 9/4; (c) 1/2; (d) −1; (e) 1; (f) 1; (g) 0; (h) 0.','(a) 1/(2√x), x > 0; (b) (n/m)aⁿ⁻ᵐ, a ≠ 0; (c) p²/q², q ≠ 0; (d) 1/2; (e) e⁻¹; (f) e²; (g) e⁻¹. See steps for exceptional parameter cases.','(i) Suggested inverted absolute-value/piecewise affine profile; exact model unverified. (ii) Quadratic, downward-opening parabola.']
CLARIFICATIONS={1:'The key says “does not exist” for (a), meaning no finite real limit. The learning solution records the more precise divergence to −∞.',3:'The source key prints 5900 for (a). The stated model at week 5 gives 38600/7 ≈ 5514.29, matching its part (b). Part (c) approaches week 16, not infinity, and gives 5200.',5:'The key prints “does not exist” for (d), but cancellation gives the finite limit 1/2. For (f), the printed question has exponent 1/x² and gives e²; the key prints e^(1/2). In (b), its generic formula needs a ≠ 0 and positive integer powers. Exceptional parameter cases are explained separately.'}
